course: dictionary
lesson: 1678
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning. The word chord has three, and the sentence around it tells you which one to use. «Songs often share a few notes or chords, because music uses a limited number of notes.» Here chords are groups of notes played together.
explain: Now read this: «A band is a team where everyone has a job: a guitar or keyboard plays chords, and someone sings.» The word chords sits next to instruments and singing, so it is about music. Clues like these are context, and they point you to the right meaning.
explain: In maths, a chord is a straight line joining two points on a circle. A sentence about circles would send you to that meaning. Always check: does my meaning fit in the sentence? If it does not, try the next meaning.
fact: A chord in music is a group of notes played at the same time, such as C, E and G on a piano.
fact: Major chords sound happy and minor chords sound sad.
fact: In maths, a chord is a straight line joining two points on a circle or curve.
fact: The longest chord of a circle is the diameter.
fact: To strike a chord means to remind someone of something or make them feel sympathy, as in «a story that strikes a chord» feels familiar.
exercise: «Many pop songs share the same four chords in the same order.» What is a chord here? | A short story | A drum beat | A straight line joining two points on a circle | *A group of notes played at the same time
exercise: In maths, what is a chord? | A dot marking the centre of a circle | *A straight line joining two points on a circle | A triangle with three equal sides
exercise: «A story that strikes a chord feels familiar.» What does strike a chord mean? | To play a wrong note | To hit a drum very hard | To draw a circle | *To remind someone of something
test: «The guitarist played a chord, then a second chord.» Which meaning fits here? | A straight line joining two points on a circle | A type of cake | A rope tied to a boat | *A group of notes played together
test: The longest chord of a circle is called what? | *A diameter | An arc | A radius | A tangent
exam: «Major chords sound happy, but minor chords sound sad.» What does this tell you about chords? | They only belong to maths | They are always the same in every song | *They can change how a song feels | They are a kind of drum
